{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791122162,"nonce":"HYOt17Uol2A2k+z4PkfRysl81aY=","title":"Measurement ignores fallback-font advances, so text with an emoji measures short","message":"TextRenderer::prepare_text_with_style shapes a glyph missing from the\nprimary font in the emoji or symbol font and shifts everything after it\nby fallback_advance - primary_advance. Measurement does not: both\nFontTextMeasurer (blinc_layout text_measurer.rs) and\nTextLayoutEngine::layout use the primary font only. Text containing an\nemoji or a fallback-chain symbol therefore measures narrower than it\ndraws, and Blinc's taffy text leaves are sized short.\n\nWhat would fix it for both sides: one public blinc_text function that\nlays out a string in a face at a size and returns per-glyph byte offsets\nand x positions with the fallback advances applied, using the same chain\nand order as the renderer. The renderer takes its positions from it,\nFontTextMeasurer and the line breaker take widths from it.\n\nRequested by the ashui session, which hits the same gap through\nTextLayoutEngine for caret stops and inline text flow, where each run's\nwidth places the next piece on the line. Tracked there as 3b62772c.","files":null}]}